# KSP coverage

Generated by `tools/ksp_coverage.py` from [KSP_SYMBOLS.md](KSP_SYMBOLS.md) (Kontakt 8 KSP Reference Manual), the installed corpus and the sampler-ksp sources. Regenerate after every KSP change; do not edit by hand.

Columns: **corpus** = instruments whose scripts mention the symbol; **parse** = the frontend knows the name (`family` = accepted by prefix as an opaque id); **lower** = how corpus call sites lower (Native executed, Approximate documented approximation, Effect/Host handed to the host through the outbox, Ignored warned and dropped, `-` = never lowered in the corpus); **runtime** = what the engine does; **UI** = the interface model reads it; **test** = a test names it. Counts are text matches, not proofs of reachability.


